        <title type="html"><![CDATA[HTTP Cache-Control stale-while-revalidate is standard]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/26895</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/26895"/>
        <updated>2025-06-01T02:44:35.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><p dir="auto">The <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Reference/Headers/Cache-Control#stale-while-revalidate" rel="nofollow">stale-while-revalidate</a> indicates non standard, but it is in the linked standard.</p>
<p dir="auto">Note that this standard also has <code class="notranslate">stale-if-error</code>. As far as I can tell that isn't supported in any browsers, but the CDNs etc widely support it.</p>
<p dir="auto">Fell out of looking at <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="3089389467" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/39674" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/issues/39674/hovercard?comment_id=2907943249&amp;comment_type=issue_comment" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/39674#issuecomment-2907943249">mdn/content#39674 (comment)</a></p>]]></content>
